works internally\nL20:   15. 【18†8. How Salsa works】\nL21:   16. 【19†9. Videos】\nL22:   17. 【20†10. Plumbing】\nL23:   18.     1. 【21†10.1. Databases and runtime】\nL24:     2. 【22†10.2. The db lifetime on tracked/interned structs】\nL25:     3. 【23†10.3. Tracked structures】\nL26:     4. 【24†10.4. Query operations】\nL27:     5.       1. 【25†10.4.1. maybe changed after】\nL28:       2. 【26†10.4.2. Fetch】\nL29:       3. 【27†10.4.3. Derived queries flowchart】\nL30:       4. 【28†10.4.4. Cycle handling】\nL31:     6. 【29†10.5. Terminology】\nL32:     7.       1. 【30†10.5.1. Backdate】\nL33:       2. 【31†10.5.2. Changed at】\nL34:       3. 【32†10.5.3. Dependency】\nL35:       4. 【33†10.5.4. Derived query】\nL36:       5. 【34†10.5.5. Durability】\nL37:       6. 【35†10.5.6. Input query】\nL38:       7. 【36†10.5.7. Ingredient】\nL39:       8. 【37†10.5.8. LRU】\nL40:       9. 【38†10.5.9. Memo】\nL41:       10. 【39†10.5.10. Query】\nL42:       11. 【40†10.5.11. Query function】\nL43:       12. 【41†10.5.12. Revision】\nL44:       13. 【42†10.5.13. Salsa item】\nL45:       14. 【43†10.5.14. Salsa struct】\nL46:       15. 【44†10.5.15. Untracked dependency】\nL47:       16. 【45†10.5.16. Verified】\nL48:   19.   20. Appendices\nL49:   21. 【46†11. Meta: about the book itself】\nL50: # Salsa\nL51: # 【47†On-Demand (Lazy) Inputs】\nL52: \nL53: Salsa inputs work best if you can easily provide all of the inputs upfront. However sometimes the set of inputs is not known beforehand.\nL54: \nL55: A typical example is reading files from disk. While it is possible to eagerly scan a particular directory and create an in-memory file tree as salsa input structs, a more straight-forward approach is to read the files lazily. That is, when a query requests the text of a file for the first time:\nL56:   1. Read the file from disk and cache it.\nL57:   2. Setup a file-system watcher for this path.\nL58:   3. Update the cached file when the watcher sends a change notification.\nL59: \nL60: This is possible to achieve in salsa, by caching the inputs in your database structs and adding a method to the database trait to retrieve them out of this cache.\nL61: \nL62: A complete, runnable file-watching example can be found in 【48†the lazy-input example†github.com】.\nL63: The setup looks roughly like this:\nL64: \nL65:     `#[salsa::input]\nL66:     struct File {\nL67:         #[returns(deref)]\nL68:         path: PathBuf,\nL69:         #[returns(deref)]\nL70:         contents: String,\nL71:     }\nL72: \nL73:     #[salsa::db]\nL74:     trait Db: salsa::Database {\nL75:         fn input(&self, path: PathBuf) -> Result<File>;\nL76:     }\nL77: \nL78:     #[salsa::db]\nL79:     #[derive(Clone)]\nL80:     struct LazyInputDatabase {\nL81:         storage: Storage<Self>,\nL82:         logs: Arc<Mutex<Vec<String>>>,\nL83:         files: DashMap<PathBuf, File>,\nL84:         file_watcher: Arc<Mutex<Debouncer<RecommendedWatcher>>>,\nL85:     }\nL86: \nL87:     impl LazyInputDatabase {\nL88:         fn new(tx: Sender<DebounceEventResult>) -> Self {\nL89:             let logs: Arc<Mutex<Vec<String>>> = Default::default();\nL90:             Self {\nL91:                 storage: Storage::new(Some(Box::new({\nL92:                     let logs = logs.clone();\nL93:                     move |event| {\nL94:                         // don't log boring events\nL95:                         if let salsa::EventKind::WillExecute { .. } = event.kind {\nL96:                             logs.lock().unwrap().push(format!(\"{event:?}\"));\nL97:                         }\nL98:                     }\nL99:                 }))),\nL100:                 logs,\nL101:                 files: DashMap::new(),\nL102:                 file_watcher: Arc::new(Mutex::new(\nL103:                     new_debouncer(Duration::from_secs(1), move |events| {\nL104:                         tx.send(events).unwrap()\nL105:                     })\nL106:                     .unwrap(),\nL107:                 )),\nL108:             }\nL109:         }\nL110:     }\nL111: \nL112:     #[salsa::db]\nL113:     impl salsa::Database for LazyInputDatabase {}\nL114: \nL115:     #[salsa::db]\nL116:     impl Db for LazyInputDatabase {\nL117:         fn input(&self, path: PathBuf) -> Result<File> {\nL118:             let path = path\nL119:                 .canonicalize()\nL120:                 .wrap_err_with(|| format!(\"Failed to read {}\", path.display()))?;\nL121:             Ok(match self.files.entry(path.clone()) {\n"
